Subject: [PATCH] minimum arm64: drop Installer from the live medium

The live medium (`RENKU_LIVE_BUILD=1`) is meant to be run straight off the
medium -- that is the whole point of splitting it from the USB install
medium in `0042`. Installer has nothing to do there: there is no install
to make.

Filters "Installer" out of both `SYSTEM_APPS` and `DESKBAR_APPLICATIONS`
when `RENKU_LIVE_BUILD=1`, the same jam variable `0042` already gates R
Chromium's inclusion on. `data/launch/user`'s own create-installer-link
job (the one that puts an Installer shortcut on the Desktop on a
read-only/live boot) already gates on `file_exists /boot/system/apps/
Installer`, so dropping the binary here is enough on its own to stop that
shortcut from appearing too -- no change needed there.

diff --git a/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum b/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum
index 9c6fd187..71cb51ab 100644
--- a/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum
+++ b/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum
@@ -160,6 +160,31 @@ DESKBAR_APPLICATIONS =
 	Terminal
 ;

+# The live medium (RENKU_LIVE_BUILD=1, set by build-renku-arm64-iso.sh) is
+# meant to be run straight off the medium, never installed from -- that is
+# what the separate USB install medium is for. Installer has nothing to do
+# there, so it comes off both lists; data/launch/user's own
+# create-installer-link job already gates on file_exists, so dropping it
+# here is enough to stop that desktop shortcut from appearing too.
+if $(RENKU_LIVE_BUILD) = 1 {
+	local filteredSystemApps ;
+	local app ;
+	for app in $(SYSTEM_APPS) {
+		if $(app) != Installer {
+			filteredSystemApps += $(app) ;
+		}
+	}
+	SYSTEM_APPS = $(filteredSystemApps) ;
+
+	local filteredDeskbarApps ;
+	for app in $(DESKBAR_APPLICATIONS) {
+		if $(app) != Installer {
+			filteredDeskbarApps += $(app) ;
+		}
+	}
+	DESKBAR_APPLICATIONS = $(filteredDeskbarApps) ;
+}
+
 DESKBAR_DESKTOP_APPLETS =
 	NetworkStatus
 	ProcessController
